HoneyCord patch for Chromium's build/toolchain/win/tool_wrapper.py
=================================================================

Problem: on a German Windows host, link.exe emits cp1252-encoded status
lines like "Bibliothek "./libwebrtc.dll.lib" und Objekt ... werden
erstellt." The default tool_wrapper.py decodes link.exe output as strict
UTF-8 and raises UnicodeDecodeError, aborting the link AFTER the .dll
was already created -- so ninja reports failure on a successful build.

Fix: try utf-8 first, fall back to cp1252, then 'replace' as a last
resort. Also swallow the German "Bibliothek ..." status line the same
way we swallow the English "Creating library ..." line.

This patch is NOT in the libwebrtc fork because tool_wrapper.py lives in
the Chromium-build subtree pulled in by gclient, not in webrtc itself.
Apply by hand to <webrtc-src>/build/toolchain/win/tool_wrapper.py before
running gn gen / ninja.

--- a/build/toolchain/win/tool_wrapper.py
+++ b/build/toolchain/win/tool_wrapper.py
@@ -140,11 +140,22 @@ class WinTool(object):
     # Read output one line at a time as it shows up to avoid OOM failures when
     # GBs of output is produced.
     for line in link.stdout:
-      line = line.decode('utf8')
+      # HoneyCord patch: link.exe on a German Windows emits cp1252 strings
+      # ("Bibliothek ... werden erstellt."). Strict utf8 throws — fall back
+      # to cp1252, then 'replace' so we never abort the link over a glyph.
+      try:
+        line = line.decode('utf8')
+      except UnicodeDecodeError:
+        try:
+          line = line.decode('cp1252')
+        except UnicodeDecodeError:
+          line = line.decode('utf8', errors='replace')
       if (not line.startswith('   Creating library ')
           and not line.startswith('Generating code')
-          and not line.startswith('Finished generating code')):
+          and not line.startswith('Finished generating code')
+          and not line.startswith('   Bibliothek ')):
         print(line.rstrip())
     return link.wait()
